From c33445f1051d9f209bead0de90cfe90da8e58e30 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sachin <sachinbarange86@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 04:27:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Disable camera usage and settings reporting

SettingUploadJobService armed a persisted job (id 17495010) that required
network and re-armed itself from its own worker, so settings left the device
long after the camera was closed. The service is now disabled in the manifest
and its scheduler entry point only cancels a job left over from an earlier
build.

MiStatsWrapper.initTrack gated OneTrack creation on camera.camera_statistic,
which defaulted to true. The gate is now hard-false, so no OneTrack instance
is created; TrackWrapper already returns early while Ib/c.a is false, which
keeps every event off the network.
